# Finance & schema

## Formulas (`finance.ts`)

```
X = incomes, Y = expenses, Z = X − Y
// allowanceSplit splits Y and Z: equal | income (∝ Barney:Lucka; Other excluded)
// discretionarySurplus = Z (analytics “pocket” / partner “keeps” pool)
```

Always build months with `buildMonthlyRecord(draft, split)` / `computeMonthly(..., split)`. Use `round2` for money.
Money display is always EUR (`CURRENCY_SYMBOL` / `CURRENCY_LOCALE` in `number.ts`) — do not re-add currency Settings.
UI: **Incomes** / **Expenses** (schema still `inflows` / `outflows`). Incomes are only three buckets: Barney / Lucka / Other. No `childSupport` field.
Split toggle: Settings + Track editor bar (`settings.allowanceSplit`).
No allocations or portfolio snapshot on `MonthlyRecord` (dropped; migrate strips legacy fields).

Banks live in `settings.banks`; cards in `settings.cards` (`bankId` required). Card `owner`: `partnerA` | `partnerB` | `common`. Labels → categories are `settings.categoryMappings` scoped by `bankId` (shared across all cards of that bank — e.g. every Revolut card). Track expenses are **card-first** (`CardExpenses`): clickable cards → that bank’s label amounts → merge into `outflows` **and** bump `paymentByOwner[owner]` via `card-expenses.ts` / MonthEditor; month category totals are a read-only rollup (no manual category grid). Settlement = effective paid (personal + split of common) vs expense fair share (`settleExpenseShares`). Sheet remounts when the editor `monthKey` changes (clears unapplied amounts); **Save month** / Ctrl+S flush any still-pending sheet via `CardExpensesHandle.flush`.

Category rename/add/remove via Settings: `updateState` runs `alignHistoryToCategories` + `alignDraftToCategories` (names on months follow Settings; analytics reads those names). Stock defaults include `investments`; migrate appends missing defaults. Demo months key by category id and take current names from `buildDemoHistory(categories)`.

- Savings rate = (X − Y) / X
- Month keys: `YYYY-MM`

## Schema changes

1. Update `types/tandem.ts`
2. Extend `migrateState` / `normalizeV1`
3. Fail closed on unknown `version`

## Demo data

Synthetic H1 2026 only (`2026-01`–`2026-06`). Load/clear via store; never replace with real household numbers in repo.
